  "_note": "Body + hands + face mapping for ARP rigs with the MODERN Facial 2 module. v1 (clean rebuild) verified against a freshly-generated stock ARP Facial 2 rig (NEW ARP rig_analysis.json) — no character-specific bones, only what ARP generates by default. EYES: LeftEye/RightEye -> c_eye_target.l/.r (LOC -> Damped Track converts to eye rotation). LIDS: LeftUpperLid/RightUpperLid -> c_eyelid_top.l/.r and similar for lower; segments c_eyelid_top_01/02/03.l cascade from these masters via ACTION constraints in the rig. BROWS: 4 source brow muscle bones per side drive the 4 brow segment widgets directly (outer to inner: LeftBrowMuscle -> c_eyebrow_03.l, LeftBrowMuscle1 -> c_eyebrow_02.l, LeftBrowMuscle2 -> c_eyebrow_01.l, LeftBrowMuscle3 -> c_eyebrow_01_end.l). The segments are CHILDREN of c_eyebrow_full.l, so c_eyebrow_full is left undriven (otherwise its motion would cascade to the segments via parent inheritance, double-counting). NOSE: c_nose_03.x and c_nose_02.x. c_nose_01.x is the parent of c_nose_02.x; leaving c_nose_01 undriven means c_nose_02 basis applies cleanly without parent cascade. CHEEKS: LeftCheekUpper -> c_cheek_smile.l (zygomatic lift), LeftCheekLower -> c_cheek_inflate.l (cheek puff, spatially the closest stock target to the source's lower-cheek position). LIPS: drive the user-facing widgets directly (stock ARP has no _master parent bones — those were Tifa-character-specific). Upper lip + lip corners use BASIS. Lower lip widgets (c_lips_bot.x, c_lips_bot_01.l/.r) parent through c_lips_bot_offset.x -> jawbone.x = 100% jaw cascade; HEAD_LOCAL on those pairs so the pb.matrix setter back-solves the basis through the jaw rotation. JAW: JawTip -> c_jawbone.x with channels=LOC (ARP converts the translation to jaw rotation internally; JawTip is the source jaw-chain child that swings when source jaw_master rotates). CHIN + TONGUE: c_chin_01/02.x and c_tong_01/02/03.x parent through jawbone.x, so HEAD_LOCAL for both. face_capture_compensation OFF + all amplifications at 1.0 by default — character-specific tuning is user-facing via the Amplification Values panel.",
